          dealing: '5 cards each. Remainder face-down.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Each player has five pegs; the winners are the first team to move all their pegs from their START area to their HOME areas.',
          gameplay: '1. Draw 1, play 1, move. 2. To come out: Jack/Q/K/Ace or Joker. 3. 2-6, 9-10: move forward that many. Ace: come out or move 1. J/Q/K: come out or move 10. 7: forward 7 or split between 2 pegs. 8: move backward 8. Joker: jump to opponent/partner peg (sends opponent to start, partner to in-spot). 4. Land on opponent = send to start; land on partner = send to in-spot. 5. Must play a moving card if possible; Joker never forced.',
          keyRules: [
            '5 pegs each. Come out, go around, turn into HOME at in-spot.',
            'Joker: jump to any peg of different color; cannot move to empty hole.',
            '7: split between two pegs (1+6, 2+5, 3+4).',
            'Arizona: play then draw; move any team peg; 9 can split forward/back.',
            "All five home = move partner's pegs.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'After come-out, move 1-3 forward before using 8 backward to reach in-spot.',
          intermediate: 'Runner peg: move 4+ forward, use 8; harass opponents. Home run: partner lands on your peg at come-out, sends you to in-spot.',
          advanced: "Double play: peg in come-out; partner's runner lands, sends it home. Chain reactions with 7/9 splits.",
          tips: [
            '8 backward from start = corner (risky).',
            'Joker: target opponent pegs near home.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
